1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,000
[roaring]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,000
[narrator] Strange beasts

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
and monsters.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vast riches.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hidden treasures.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Evil haunts.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Uncharted frontiers.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
“The mysterious unknown.”

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The people who are captivated
by the magic in those words…

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
are called…

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Hunters.

12
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
[theme song playing]

13
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,000
[seagull squawking]

14
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:18,000
LETTER x FROM x GON

15
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
"Dear Aunt Mito and Grandma.

16
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,000
How are you doing?

17
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,000
I’m doing pretty okay myself."

18
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,000
[chuckles]

19
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,000
"I just passed
the Third Phase of the Hunter Exam.

20
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Isn't that great?

21
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,000
[in unison with Gon's voice] But it's been
pretty tough getting this far.

22
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Right after I left the island...

23
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,000
[Gon's voice] the boat I was traveling on
ran into a really big storm.

24
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,000
[thunder]

25
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,000
[Gon] It wasn’t all bad, though.

26
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
That’s where I met Leorio and Kurapika.

27
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,000
If only you could buy class, as well.
Leorio.

28
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
That was strike three.

29
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Step outside.

30
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,000
Time to finish off
the filthy Kurta bloodline

31
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,000
once and for all.

32
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Take that back, Leorio!

33
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,000
I said take it back.

34
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,000
It’s Mister Leorio.

35
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Take back what you said about my clan!

36
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,000
I will forgive you if you repent, Leorio.

37
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
You owe me an apology.

38
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
And I’m not telling you again.

39
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
I’m not repenting for anything, hear me?

40
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Very well.

41
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
-[screaming]
-[gasps]

42
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
[both] Damn!

43
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Thanks, Gon. You’re incredible!

44
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,000
You saved my life back there.

45
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,000
Well, I didn’t do it all alone.

46
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
Those two over there
helped rescue you too.

47
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,000
He’s right. Thank you both!

48
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,000
Please. No thanks necessary.

49
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Yeah. No prob.

50
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,000
We’re just glad to see
you made it okay!

51
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Me too!

52
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:38,000
In fact, I ought to get back to my post
right away!

53
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,000
[chuckles quietly]

54
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,000
[Kurapika giggles]

55
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,000
What’s so funny?

56
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,000
I’m embarrassed at my behavior.

57
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Pardon my rudeness, Mister Leorio.

58
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,000
I wasn’t expecting that.

59
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Just forget it.

60
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,000
You can drop the ‘Mister.’ Leorio’s fine.

61
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
I’m sorry, too.

62
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:04,000
And I take back everything
that I said to you before.

63
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,000
That was wrong of me.

64
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:10,000
[Gon] That’s what led to the three of us
traveling together

65
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:14,000
and we headed off
to find the site of the Hunter Exam.

66
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,000
[bird cawing]

67
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,000
[Gon] But...

68
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:20,000
the journey wasn’t easy at all.

69
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:29,000
Time for the exciting
multiple-choice quiz!

70
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
[various instruments play]

71
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
-And now here is your question.
-[beep]

72
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,000
You learn both your son and your daughter
have been kidnapped.

73
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
You will only be able
to rescue one of them.

74
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Choose one for your son

75
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,000
and two for your daughter.

76
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Which of these two will you rescue?

77
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:47,000
[growls]

78
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,000
[Leorio] She’s messing with us!

79
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:55,000
[roaring]

80
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,000
Out of the way, Kurapika!

81
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:02,000
This old hag needs to be taught a lesson
and I’m gonna make sure she gets it!

82
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,000
Would you please calm down?

83
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,000
How the hell do you expect me
to calm down?!

84
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:09,000
We got it right! Do you really want
to jeopardize that?

85
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,000
We did?

86
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,000
We’ve already given the correct response.

87
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,000
Silence.

88
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,000
Any other answer
would have been incorrect.

89
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Please, save her!

90
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,000
You have to save my wife!

91
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Leorio! See to his injuries.

92
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,000
Kurapika!

93
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,000
[sighs]

94
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:43,000
So… who’re you?

95
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,000
Hold on.

96
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:50,000
How can you tell that I’m not
the same one from before?

97
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Huh? Oh, well, you look totally different.

98
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,000
Your voice is different, too.

99
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,000
It’s higher and kinda thinner.

100
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,000
[chortles]

101
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,000
[laughs loudly]

102
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:07,000
What’s up? Why are you laughing?
Is it something I said?

103
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:12,000
Your superhuman physical ability
and your powers of observation defy logic.

104
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,000
You, too, are worthy
to take the Hunter Exam.

105
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,000
So, you pass.

106
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,000
[Leorio chuckles]

107
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,000
[Gon] Then...

108
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,000
the Hunter Exam finally began!

109
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,000
I apologize for the delay.

110
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Thank you for waiting.

111
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:44,000
The entry period for Hunter applicants
is officially closed.

112
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,000
So, with no further ado...

113
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,000
the Hunter Exam will now begin!

114
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,000
The first phase is quite simple.

115
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:03,000
All you have to do
is follow me to the second phase.

116
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:05,000
So, try to keep up.

117
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,000
[Gon] That’s when I made friends
with a boy I met.

118
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:12,000
His name’s Killua
and he’s about the same age as me.

119
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,000
-[Killua] Hey. How old are you?
-Twelve years old.

120
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,000
Same as me.

121
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,000
I think I’ll run for a little while.

122
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
Whoa! Cool!

123
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,000
My name’s Killua.

124
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,000
Hi, I’m Gon!

125
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:37,000
[Gon]
Hey why do you want to be a Hunter anyway?

126
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
Who, me?

127
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,000
I never said I wanted to be a Hunter.

128
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,000
I just heard the Exam
was supposed to be really hard.

129
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,000
It sounded kinda fun, so here I am.

130
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,000
But it’s not as fun as I thought.

131
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,000
What about you?

132
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:54,000
[Gon]
Well, the thing is my dad’s a Hunter.

133
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:58,000
So, I decided I was gonna be a Hunter
just like him, no matter what!

134
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:01,000
[Killua] Hmm.
So, what kind of Hunter is he?

135
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:02,000
[Gon] No idea.

136
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,000
-It’s the weirdest thing I’ve ever heard!
-Huh?

137
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:09,000
You want to be the same kind of Hunter
as your dad

138
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:11,000
but you don’t know anything about him?
That’s nuts!

139
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:14,000
Mito’s the one who raised me
and she told me a little,

140
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:17,000
but I’ve only ever seen him in pictures
she showed me from a long time ago.

141
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:20,000
-Wait, so who’s Mito?
-She’s my aunt.

142
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:21,000
Ah.

143
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:25,000
She said that my dad took the Hunter Exam
when he was only 12 years old, too.

144
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:28,000
He passed his first try
and became a Hunter.

145
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,000
That's when he decided
to leave the island.

146
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,000
So, I came here in order to find out
why he chose being a Hunter

147
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
over staying at home with me.

148
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Hm...

149
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,000
[examinee] The exit!

150
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,000
Oh, thank goodness!

151
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:50,000
[both] Goal!

152
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Yeah! I did it! I finished first!

153
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,000
What are you talking about? I totally won.

154
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:05,000
Now, let’s go over the rules of the game.

155
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:08,000
All you have to do
is simply take this ball away from me.

156
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:13,000
If you can do that
before the airship arrives, you win.

157
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
[both] I’ve almost got it!

158
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,000
[Gon] Whoa!

159
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:40,000
Well now.

160
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:45,000
Excellent teamwork!
You get an ‘A’ for effort!

161
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,000
The Hunter Exam’s...

162
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:52,000
[in unison with Gon's voice]
...been a lot of fun with Killua around.

163
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:54,000
We’re best friends now,
so that’s pretty cool.

164
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:03,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

165
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:08,000
LETTER

166
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,000
[Gon] Besides Killua,

167
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,000
there are applicants
from all over the world

168
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
who came to take the Hunter Exam,

169
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,000
so there are lots of amazing people.

170
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,000
[appreciative exhale]

171
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,000
Not bad,

172
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,000
little boy.

173
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Is that a fishing pole?

174
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:37,000
How original!

175
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,000
I’d like to see it. Do you mind?

176
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,000
[Leorio] Leave him alone.

177
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:47,000
[yells] Your fight’s with me!

178
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
[roaring]

179
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,000
[Hisoka]
Did you come here to help your friend?

180
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,000
[gasps]

181
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:03,000
Such a good boy.

182
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,000
I adore that look.

183
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:10,000
[grunting]

184
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,000
Well done.

185
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,000
I’m beginning to get excited.

186
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,000
[roaring]

187
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:34,000
[Gon choking]

188
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:37,000
[Hisoka] It’s so delightful.

189
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:41,000
I love that look!

190
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,000
[coughing]

191
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:51,000
[Hisoka] Don't worry.

192
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:55,000
I didn’t kill your friend.
He’s going to be just fine.

193
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,000
And that’s because he passed!

194
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,000
[Hisoka chuckling]

195
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:05,000
And yes.

196
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,000
You pass as well.

197
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,000
Now, go and become a good Hunter.

198
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,000
[Gon] But I’ve gotta say.

199
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,000
It was actually pretty exciting
back there.

200
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:24,000
I was so scared that all I wanted to do
was run away.

201
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,000
But I couldn’t.

202
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:28,000
‘cause I was excited at the same time.

203
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Isn’t that weird?

204
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:39,000
There were 404 applicants
at the start of the Hunter Exam

205
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,000
but by the time
we reached the Third Phase,

206
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,000
there were only 41 left.

207
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,000
[Beans] Ah… Ahem.

208
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:50,000
Everyone. This is the site
of the Exam’s Third Phase.

209
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:53,000
You’ll be competing here
at the top of the Trick Tower.

210
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Did you say, ‘Trick Tower’?

211
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
[Beans] In order to pass this Phase

212
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:00,000
you must
reach the base of the tower alive.

213
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:03,000
The time limit is 72 hours.

214
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,000
[Leorio] Whoa. Where the hell are we?

215
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,000
See that? Over there.

216
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,000
[Lippo] Gentlemen, let me explain.

217
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:23,000
You’ve probably already noticed

218
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:26,000
that some of the prisoners of Trick Tower
are standing before you.

219
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:29,000
Not just prisoners.

220
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:32,000
The Hunter Exam Committee
has also officially hired them on

221
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,000
as Examiners.

222
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:38,000
In this Phase you’ll be fighting
against all five of them.

223
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:41,000
Without knowing what’s up their sleeves,

224
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:43,000
there’s far too much at stake.

225
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,000
-Given that, I’ll-
-[Tonpa] Nope. I’ll go.

226
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:49,000
Mister Tonpa?

227
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
[Tonpa grunting]

228
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,000
[Bendot] Begin!

229
00:14:57,000 --> 00:15:00,000
[growling]

230
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:04,000
[yells] I... give up!

231
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:05,000
Huh?

232
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:07,000
What?

233
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,000
Did he just...

234
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:15,000
say that he gives up?

235
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:19,000
Uh maybe he meant ‘give me a sec’…

236
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
[chuckles lightly]

237
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:27,000
We each light a candle at the same time

238
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:30,000
and whoever’s candle goes out first
is the loser.

239
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:33,000
[startled cry]

240
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:37,000
Hey. Take a look at Gon’s candle.

241
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:39,000
The flame suddenly got a lot stronger!

242
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,000
I should’ve known.

243
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:45,000
He somehow laced Gon’s candle
with gunpowder or some other accelerant.

244
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,000
That’s why it’s burning so much faster!

245
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,000
I guess now that the flame’s burning
so much stronger,

246
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,000
it’ll take a lot more than a little breeze
to put it out.

247
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,000
[Sedokan gasps]

248
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,000
He’s fast!

249
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,000
[Gon blows the candle]

250
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,000
[chuckles]

251
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:07,000
I win!

252
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,000
Look at his tattoo;

253
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,000
it’s a spider with twelve legs!

254
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,000
And that means…

255
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Name’s Majitani!

256
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:25,000
I’m one of the Phantom Troupe’s
four devas!

257
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:27,000
That first strike
was just an introduction.

258
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,000
This is your last chance to give up.

259
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:33,000
If you do, I’m still willing to...

260
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,000
Hey… What’s wrong with you?

261
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,000
What are you--

262
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,000
Huh?

263
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:55,000
[strangled cries]

264
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:15,000
All right! I know what we’re betting on!

265
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:18,000
Let’s bet on
who’ll win rock paper scissors!

266
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:21,000
[giggles]

267
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,000
Hey, what’s so funny?

268
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:26,000
[Leroute] It’s just I can already tell
what you’re going to use.

269
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,000
I’m something of a mind reader, you see.

270
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,000
That’s a lie!

271
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:32,000
You can bluff all you want,

272
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:35,000
but it’ll take a lot more than that
to scare me!

273
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:36,000
You’ll believe it soon…

274
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,000
[grunts]

275
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:41,000
-You ready?
-[cries out]

276
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:43,000
And rock! Paper!

277
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:45,000
[both] Scissors!

278
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,000
[Leroute] Well? What’ll you use next?

279
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:55,000
Come on. Think hard.

280
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:57,000
[Leroute laughs]

281
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:59,000
Damn it! [grunts]

282
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,000
[screaming]

283
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,000
What is happening?!

284
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:03,000
Here we go!

285
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,000
Here comes the draw!

286
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:13,000
[laughs]

287
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:15,000
I win! Yay!

288
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,000
How do you wanna do this?

289
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:22,000
[man] Do this?

290
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,000
You have the wrong idea.

291
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:28,000
See, you’re about to be on the wrong side
of a one-sided massacre.

292
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:32,000
I don’t care about the Exam
or reducing my sentence.

293
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,000
All I want is to hear you scream.

294
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:38,000
Really? Fine.

295
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,000
We’ll just keep fighting
until one of us dies.

296
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:43,000
That’s right. A battle to the death.

297
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:47,000
Soon... I’ll tear your body apart

298
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,000
with just my bare hands. You got it?

299
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,000
[heart beating]

300
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,000
[all gasp]

301
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:08,000
[heart beating]

302
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:13,000
That’s mine.

303
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:14,000
[grunts]

304
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:16,000
It belongs to me.

305
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Give it back.

306
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,000
Give it to me.

307
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:37,000
[announcer] Please select a path.

308
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:40,000
There are two available options
to choose from.

309
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:43,000
The long and difficult path
which the entire group can take,

310
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:46,000
or the short and easy path

311
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:48,000
which will be limited
to only three of you.

312
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:53,000
I’m going to press ‘O’.

313
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:57,000
It’s just we all made it this far
by working together.

314
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,000
We should finish together.

315
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Gon…

316
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:02,000
[Gon] It’s a big risk. I know that.

317
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,000
But still, we’ve got to try!

318
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,000
[grunting]

319
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:19,000
[Gon]
We entered the long and difficult path,

320
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,000
broke down the wall

321
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:24,000
and from there,
we snuck into the short and easy one.

322
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:34,000
Boy, my butt hurts!

323
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:38,000
I certainly wasn’t expecting
the short and easy path to be a slide.

324
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:41,000
[Hisoka] Three of them, eh?

325
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:43,000
[announcer] Thirty seconds remain.

326
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:46,000
Even with that big slide,
that was really close!

327
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:48,000
My hands are covered in blisters.

328
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,000
[Leorio] Same here.

329
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:55,000
[announcer] Leorio, number 403,
is the twenty-third to pass.

330
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:57,000
My hands are wrecked

331
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
but all five of us
cleared the tower together, didn’t we?

332
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:02,000
And it’s all thanks to Gon!

333
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,000
[long signal sounds]

334
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:10,000
[announcer] The Third Phase
of the Hunter Exam is over!

335
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:12,000
Twenty-five applicants have passed,

336
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:14,000
including one deceased.

337
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:21,000
[Gon] That’s pretty much it, Aunt Mito.

338
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:24,000
That’s how I completed
the Third Phase of the Exam.

339
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:28,000
I don’t know how many phases
are left to go

340
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:31,000
but I’m gonna pass every last one of ‘em.

341
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:32,000
‘cause I’m gonna be a Hunter...

342
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:35,000
just like Dad.

343
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:37,000
Until next time!

344
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:39,000
Gon Freecss.

345
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:49,000
[Mito] Well, did you hear that, Ging?

346
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:52,000
It looks like your son is following
in your footsteps.

347
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:57,000
So? Are you happy?

348
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:02,000
[theme song playing]

349
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,000
[Gon] Next time: "Hit x The x Target!"

350
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:29,000
A sneaky hit!

351
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:31,000
[Hisoka] Hit and run.
